# Personnel example #2: Parenthesis, completed 2026-10-22.
# Base: main at 6cf26319ab2f8b89706677ccfacd83fddb2de46b.
# Original table layout: position details first, funding distribution on expand.
# FE Start / FE End retain the shared UC Path tooltip labels.
# Differences show current funding totals above full job amounts.
# Funding amounts use base-content; full job amounts use base-content/80 in ( ).
# Discrepancy amounts have no tooltip or special font weight.
# Footer always shows funding totals above full job totals in parentheses,
# with identical font size and weight and only the text color differing.
# Future and unavailable funding amounts are excluded from funding totals.
# Expanded funding columns share the parent table's column widths.
# Funding title and first column align with the employee name via pl-8.
# Personnel descriptions explain that parentheses include non-PI funding.
# Restore selectively against subsequent edits rather than blindly applying.

